---
import BlogLayout from "../../layouts/BlogLayout.astro";

const title = "Pakistan Salary Tax Guide: Tax on Salary for Salaried Individuals";
const description = "Pakistan salary tax guide for salaried individuals. Learn how tax on salary is calculated under FBR rules, Section 149 deductions, and calculate take-home pay.";
const image = "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1524492412937-b28074a5d7da?w=1200&q=80";
const canonical = "https://finsiva.com/blogs/pakistan-salary-tax-guide";
const author = "Zainab Hussain";
const authorBio = "Employment tax consultant focusing on salary taxation and employer compliance.";
const lastUpdated = "August 2026";
const readTime = "9 min read";

const faqSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How is tax on salary calculated in Pakistan?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Tax on salary is calculated by taking annual gross salary, subtracting exempt allowances (medical allowance up to 10% of basic salary) and contributions, applying FBR progressive tax slabs, and dividing by 12 for monthly withholding."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is Section 149 withholding tax on salary in Pakistan?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Section 149 mandates that every employer deduct income tax from an employee's salary each month and deposit it with the FBR by the 15th of the following month."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do I still need to file a tax return if my employer deducts tax monthly?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. Monthly employer withholding satisfies payment requirements, but filing an annual tax return is mandatory to stay on the Active Taxpayer List (ATL) and claim refunds for excess tax deducted."
      }
    }
  ]
};
---

<BlogLayout title={title} description={description} image={image} canonical={canonical} author={author} authorBio={authorBio} lastUpdated={lastUpdated} readTime={readTime}>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />

  <div class="min-h-screen bg-canvas dark:bg-canvas">
    <main class="min-h-screen">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="mb-6 text-sm">
          <ol class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><a href="/" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">Home</a></li>
            <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="text-muted" aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/blogs" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">Blogs</a></li>
            <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="text-muted" aria-hidden="true">/</span><span class="font-medium text-ink dark:text-on-primary" aria-current="page">Pakistan Salary Tax Guide</span></li>
          </ol>
        </nav>

        <article class="prose max-w-none">
          <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-ink mb-4 dark:text-on-primary">Pakistan Salary Tax Guide: Tax on Salary for Salaried Individuals</h1>
          <p class="text-lg text-body dark:text-muted">Last updated: August 2026 | Verified FBR Guidelines | 9 min read</p>

          <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1454165804606-c3d57bc86b40?w=1200&q=80" alt="Salary tax calculation documents and payroll reports" class="mb-6 w-full rounded-lg object-cover max-h-80 sm:max-h-96" loading="lazy" />

          <!-- Early Calculator CTA -->
          <div class="my-6 p-6 rounded-2xl border border-primary/30 bg-primary/5 dark:border-primary/20 dark:bg-primary/5 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4">
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Calculate Your Pakistan Salary Tax & Take-Home Pay</h3>
              <p class="text-sm text-body dark:text-muted mt-1">Check your monthly tax deduction, exempt allowances, and net salary instantly.</p>
            </div>
            <a href="/countries/pakistan/income-tax/salary-tax-calculator" class="btn btn-primary text-sm font-semibold shrink-0 px-5 py-2.5">
              Launch Pakistan Salary Tax Calculator →
            </a>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-body dark:text-muted leading-relaxed">
            <p>Tax on salary in Pakistan is calculated using progressive FBR slabs and deducted monthly by your employer under <strong>Section 149</strong> of the <em>Income Tax Ordinance, 2001</em>. Employers handle the deduction, but understanding how salary tax is calculated is essential for verifying pay slips and optimizing deductions.</p>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">How Is Tax on Salary Calculated?</h2>
            <p>Employers compute monthly salary tax using the following steps:</p>
            <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-2">
              <li><strong>Project Annual Gross Salary:</strong> Estimate basic pay, allowances, bonuses, and perquisites.</li>
              <li><strong>Subtract Exempt Allowances:</strong> Medical allowance (up to 10% of basic salary) and other statutory allowances are deducted.</li>
              <li><strong>Deduct Contributions:</strong> EOBI, provident fund, and approved pension scheme contributions reduce taxable pay.</li>
              <li><strong>Apply FBR Progressive Slabs:</strong> Apply slab rates to determine total annual tax.</li>
              <li><strong>Divide by 12:</strong> Deduct equal monthly tax installments from your paycheck.</li>
            </ol>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Section 149 Withholding & Filer Status</h2>
            <p>While monthly withholding satisfies payment requirements, filing your return annually via the <a href="https://iris.fbr.gov.pk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">FBR IRIS Portal</a> places you on the Active Taxpayer List (ATL) and qualifies you for filer status discounts. Learn more in our <a href="/blogs/pakistan-income-tax-guide" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">Pakistan Income Tax Guide</a>.</p>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas p-4 dark:border-overlay-lighter dark:bg-surface">
            <p class="font-medium text-ink dark:text-on-primary">3. What is the annual tax-free income limit for salaried individuals in Pakistan?</p>
            <ul class="mt-2 list-disc pl-6 text-sm text-body dark:text-muted">
              <li>A) PKR 500,000</li>
              <li>B) PKR 550,000</li>
              <li>C) PKR 600,000</li>
              <li>D) PKR 650,000</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Further Reading</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-body dark:text-muted">
            <li><a href="https://www.fbr.gov.pk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">Federal Board of Revenue (FBR) – Official Website</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taxation_in_Pakistan" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">Taxation in Pakistan – Wikipedia</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://iris.fbr.gov.pk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">FBR IRIS Portal – Salary Tax Filing</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://www.fbr.gov.pk/forms-and-publications" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">FBR Forms and Publications Library</a></li>
          </ul>

        </article>
      </div>
    </main>
  </div>
</BlogLayout>